      "reason": "The certified data record each claimant's PIP daily living award, not the assessment points behind it, so the model leaves everyone's points at its default of -1 (not assessed) and keeps the recorded award. A change to the points needed for the standard or enhanced rate therefore moves no one. Changes to the rates themselves are not affected. A measure that changes the recorded awards is held too, as a precaution: in a year with no recorded award the model carries an earlier one forward unless newer points replace it, though its copy of the certified data records an award in every Budget year.",
